          %h1#the_axiom_of_choice The axiom of choice
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statement"} Statement
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_other_categories"} In other categories
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ExternalForm"} External form
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#internal_form"} Internal form
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_toposes"} In toposes
              %li
                %a{:href => "#equivalents"} Equivalents
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Variants"} Variants
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_higher_category_theory"} In higher category theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#InTypeTheory"} In type theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_spatial_type_theory"} In spatial type theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#consequences"} Consequences
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesInHomotopy"} In homotopy type theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_spatial_type_theory_2"} In spatial type theory
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            The
            %strong axiom of choice
            is the following statement:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
                in the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} splits
          %p
            This means: for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A \to B
            of sets, there is a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma\colon B \to A
            (a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi σ
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi B
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (B \stackrel{\sigma}{\to} A \stackrel{f}{\to} B)
                  \=
                  (B \stackrel{Id_B}{\to} B)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Note that a surjection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
            of sets can be regarded as a
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family"} family
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+sets"} inhabited sets
          %p
            When the full axiom of choice fails, it may still be valid for some restricted class of objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and/or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            such that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} splits
            is called
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that one can make choices ‘with values in’
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/choice+object"} choice object
            (this is not quite equivalent to every epimorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
            splitting).
          %h2#in_other_categories In other categories
          %p
            More generally, we may consider analogous statements in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            other than
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %h3#ExternalForm External form
          %p
            We say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            satisfies the
            %strong external axiom of choice
            if every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} splits
          %p
            In this form, the axiom of choice may look less mysterious than in its original formulation. For instance, it is clear that it fails in contexts such as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/balanced+category"} balanced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            which is not a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+epimorphism"} extremal epimorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            (and in any
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %p
            More generally still, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            may be taken to say that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to X
            admits a section. Obviously this refers only to singleton covers, but if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superextensive+site"} superextensive
            then any covering family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_i\colon U_i \to X)_i
            can be replaced by a singleton cover
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi u
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_u U_i \to X
          %h3#internal_form Internal form
          %p
            However, when working in a category that has an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack+semantics"} stack semantics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internally+projective+object"} internally projective
            = succeed "." do
              %strong internal axiom of choice
          %p
            This is generally a weaker statement: a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            satisfies the external AC if and only if it satisfies the internal AC and also (the external form of)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supports+split"} supports split
          %p
            The following characterization can be found in Freyd-Scedrov (
            %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov90"}> 1990
            , p.181)
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              satisfies the internal axiom of choice iff it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tendue"} étendue
          %p In particular, satisfaction of IAC entails Booleanness.
          %p
            Classical examples of Boolean étendues are provided by toposes of group actions hence these all satisfy IAC but satisfy AC only in case the group is trivial (cf. Johnstone
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JT77"} 1977
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov90"} 1990
          %p
            If a topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            satisfies IAC, then so do all of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/139874/pullback-stability-of-internally-projective-objects/140262#140262"} this answer
          %h3#in_toposes In toposes
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              satisfies the external axiom of choice iff it is equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              on a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Boolean+algebra"} complete Boolean algebra
          %h2#equivalents Equivalents
          %p
            The following statements are all equivalent to the axiom of choice in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            (although sometimes the proof in one direction requires
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %em very
            short list; much longer lists can be found elsewhere, such as at
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axiom_of_choice#Equivalents"} Wikipedia
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                That any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
                of any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family"} family
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+sets"} inhabited sets
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited"} inhabited
            %li
              %p
                That given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                and an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(b)
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                at
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                has a (local)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/choice+operator"} choice operator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon:[f^*(b)] \to f^*(b)
                from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support+of+a+set"} support
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(b)
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
